{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Domain requires this callback even for a storage-only consumer. The\n delegation test must use only node_path; discovering edges would be\n an unwanted graph access, which this guard rejects. Traversal fixtures\n separately exercise edge discovery."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `tests/support/stored_graph.rs` `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` is valid.\n\n- **Form:** The citation sits on an explicit function with a body. Its explanation is in fenced citation commentary, so it counts as a tracked justification.\n- **Substance:** The reason is not mere difficulty. The `Domain` trait requires the callback, and `StoredGraph` is a storage-only fixture. The function is a deliberate `panic!` guard that rejects any graph edge discovery. It is therefore never meant to run, and zero execution is expected.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The body is only `panic!(\"storage operations must not discover graph edges\")`. The other `StoredGraph` `Domain` methods (`node_path`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`) never call `outgoing_edges`.\n- **Agreement with the caller:** The delegation test in `tests/storage.rs`, `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path`, calls only `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`, `node_path` and the storage record path. It never discovers edges, which matches the commentary.\n- **Traversal fixtures:** Other `Domain` fixtures implement `outgoing_edges` with real behavior. Examples are `Memory` in `src/agent/tests.rs`, `Memory` in `src/graph/validation_tests.rs`, and `Application` in `tests/contracts.rs`. The claim that traversal fixtures exercise edge discovery is therefore supported.\n- **Redundancy:** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant.",
